---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 7, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="What this site is not a substitute for — read this before acting on anything here."
>
  <article class="post-content">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="search-intro">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This site writes about Ruqya, the unseen, jinn, sihr, the evil eye, and related topics.
      Given the subject, a few things need to be said plainly.
    </p>

    <h2>Not medical or mental health advice</h2>
    <p>
      Symptoms like anxiety, depression, insomnia, seizures, hallucinations, or sudden changes in
      behavior can have real medical or psychological causes. This site is not a diagnosis tool
      and nothing here should delay you from seeing a qualified doctor or licensed mental health
      professional. If you or someone you know is in a medical or psychiatric emergency, contact
      emergency services immediately — not this website.
    </p>

    <h2>Not a fatwa</h2>
    <p>
      Posts here reflect our understanding based on the Qur'an, authentic Sunnah, and available
      evidence, written for general reading — not an individualized religious ruling for your
      specific situation. For that, consult a qualified, trustworthy scholar who knows your
      circumstances.
    </p>

    <h2>No guaranteed outcomes</h2>
    <p>
      Ruqya, du'a, and worship are acts of devotion and reliance on Allah — not transactions with
      guaranteed results. As stated on our <a href="/about">About page</a>, we do not promise
      miracles, and no post or download on this site is a guarantee that a particular outcome
      will follow.
    </p>

    <h2>Uncertainty is labeled, not eliminated</h2>
    <p>
      We try to clearly separate what's established from what's uncertain or folklore. That
      labeling reduces the risk of relying on bad information — it doesn't eliminate it. Verify
      anything important against reliable sources or a qualified scholar before acting on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Downloadable resources</h2>
    <p>
      Files on the <a href="/downloads">Downloads</a> page (trackers, worksheets, prompts) are
      informal personal aids, not prescriptions, rulings, or clinical tools.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      Questions? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
